-- Migration 0021_matter_restriction: generated by drizzle-kit (the table), RLS, grants and function hand-written, reviewed before commit.
-- Reviewed-by: Claude (agent, #233)
-- Database side of the permission policy (#233, part of #20; spike §4.1, architecture §6.3):
--   * matter_restriction: one row per restricted (workspace, matter); allowed_user_ids lists who may
--     read it besides owners. Tenant table under FORCE RLS (tenantPolicy()). matter_id has no FK
--     until the matter table exists (Court Graph milestone).
--   * causedeck_clerk: the role `withWorkspace({ dbRole: 'clerk' })` switches to (SET LOCAL ROLE)
--     for clerk members. It is provisioned outside migrations (infra/docker/postgres/init/02-roles.sql;
--     the owner cannot CREATE ROLE), so this migration fails fast if it is missing. It gets exactly
--     the app role's current privileges (copied from the catalog, so the append-only revokes on
--     audit_event and ai_call carry over) and the same default privileges. Later migrations that
--     GRANT to causedeck_app explicitly must grant causedeck_clerk too (docs/engineering/tenancy.md).
--   * app_clerk_view(base, view_name, excluded_columns): the clerk column-scoped view pattern. It
--     creates a view of `base` without the excluded (strategy) columns, revokes every clerk privilege
--     on `base`, and grants SELECT on the view to the app and clerk roles. The view runs with its
--     owner's rights, so it refuses a base table without FORCE RLS or with a policy that names the
--     owner role (either would let the view see other workspaces). Migration-only: no EXECUTE grant.
-- New table, grants and a function only: nothing existing is altered or dropped.
DO $$
BEGIN
  IF NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM pg_roles WHERE rolname = 'causedeck_clerk') THEN
    RAISE EXCEPTION 'role causedeck_clerk is missing: create it as in infra/docker/postgres/init/02-roles.sql (see infra/docker/README.md) before running 0021_matter_restriction';
  END IF;
END
$$;--> statement-breakpoint
